# C: bonds. The Foundation controls Mozilla.org, licenses the marks to the Corporation and MZLA, funds Mozilla.ai and the Mozilla Ventures fund, and incubated Mozilla Data Collective. Each is mirrored in the other atom.
nodes:
  - id: C:bond/foundation-controls-org
    type: bond
    name: Foundation controls Mozilla.org
    summary: 'Mozilla.org stays within the umbrella of the Foundation: the Foundation appoints the majority of its board and consolidates it for financial reporting. The 2024 Form 990 Schedule R lists Mozilla.org (EIN 33-3437202) as a related tax-exempt organization whose direct controlling entity is the Foundation. Not an ownership bond: a non-profit has no shares.'
    kinds: [controls]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mozilla-org
    control: full
    basis: appoints the majority of the Mozilla.org board; consolidates it for financial reporting (Mozilla wiki, June 2026); Schedule R Part II, 2024
    accounting: consolidated
    inherits: [principles]
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/news/announcing-mozilla-org-new-non-profit/', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf'], confidence: 0.8, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/foundation-licenses-corporation
    type: bond
    name: Foundation licenses the Mozilla marks to the Corporation
    summary: 'The Corporation pays the Foundation a trademark licence royalty based on its annual royalties revenue: $22.6 million for 2024, $18.4 million for 2023.'
    kinds: [licenses]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mozilla-corporation
    control: none
    scope: ['atom/mozilla-org//C:ip/mozilla-trademarks']
    terms: royalty on the Corporation's annual royalties revenue; $22,622,178 in 2024 (Form 990 Schedule R Part V)
    pending: After the 2026 transfer the FAQ says Mozilla.org owns the trademarks; which entity is the licensor now?
    contract: C:contract/trademark-license-corporation
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf', 'https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org', 'https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/trademarks/policy/'], confidence: 0.7, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/foundation-licenses-mzla
    type: bond
    name: Foundation licenses the Thunderbird marks to MZLA
    summary: 'MZLA pays the Foundation a royalty based on revenue from certain products: $415 thousand for 2024, $267 thousand for 2023.'
    kinds: [licenses]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mzla
    control: none
    scope: ['atom/mozilla-org//C:ip/mozilla-trademarks']
    terms: royalty on revenue from certain products under a trademark license agreement
    pending: After the 2026 transfer the FAQ says Mozilla.org owns the trademarks; which entity is the licensor now?
    contract: C:contract/trademark-license-mzla
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://wiki.mozilla.org/Mozilla_org'], confidence: 0.7, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/foundation-funds-mozilla-ai
    type: bond
    name: Foundation funds Mozilla.ai
    summary: The Foundation committed $30 million to create Mozilla.ai, launched in March 2023 and still pre-revenue in the 2024 report.
    kinds: [funds]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mozilla-ai
    control: none
    terms: $30 million committed at launch, March 2023
    since: 2023-03
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/annualreport/2024/article/financing-an-open-internet-mozillas-path-forward/', 'https://mozilla.ai/company/about-us'], confidence: 0.8, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/foundation-funds-ventures
    type: bond
    name: Foundation funds the Mozilla Ventures fund
    summary: The Foundation is the sole partner in the first fund, size $35 million, announced in November 2022; the 2023 Form 990 shows capital contributions of $24,963,716 to Mozilla Ventures I, LP in 2023.
    kinds: [funds]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mozilla-ventures
    control: none
    terms: sole partner in the first fund, Mozilla Ventures I, LP; fund size $35 million
    since: 2022-11-02
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/foundation/annualreport/2024/article/financing-an-open-internet-mozillas-path-forward/', 'https://assets.mozilla.net/annualreport/2024/b200-mozilla-foundation-form-990-public-disclosure-ty23.pdf', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Foundation'], confidence: 0.8, state: known}

  - id: C:bond/foundation-incubated-mdc
    type: bond
    name: Foundation incubated Mozilla Data Collective
    summary: Mozilla Data Collective describes itself as incubated by the Mozilla Foundation; it was announced in July 2025 as a sister platform to Common Voice and registered as a UK company in February 2026.
    kinds: [affiliated]
    from: atom/mozilla-foundation
    to: atom/mozilla-data-collective
    control: none
    since: 2025-07-30
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://mozilladatacollective.com/', 'https://discourse.mozilla.org/t/exciting-news-mozilla-data-collective/145191'], confidence: 0.8, state: known}
